},"summary":"Runs a controller audit and fixture composition over Engine Room modules.","title":"Run the Engine Room fixture composition"},"claim_ceiling":"validates declared public contract only","claim_ceiling_restated":"Runs a controller audit and a fixture composition over the Engine Room modules, and rejects a run in which an expected target is missing.","claim_id":"claim::engine_room_demo","evidence_class":"semantic_validator","evidence_strength_rank":5,"organ_id":"engine_room_demo","truth_accounting_bucket":"real_import_validation","validator_command":"python -m microcosm_core.organs.engine_room_demo run --input fixtures/first_wave/engine_room_demo/input --out receipts/first_wave/engine_room_demo --acceptance-out receipts/acceptance/first_wave/engine_room_demo_fixture_acceptance.json"},"claim_clause_coverage":{"claim_text_sha256":"803dee36585b3b5457034bc188b5bc133ebd31a8c658eb87dca5a73e530cd5ce","clauses":[],"mapped_clause_count":null,"status":"unknown","whole_claim_coverage":"unknown"},"classification":{"evidence_class":"semantic_validator","family":"import_projection_and_drift","real_substrate_disposition":"real_substrate_capsule","truth_accounting_bucket":"real_import_validation"},"component_id":"engine_room_demo","evidence_state":{"current_backend_binding":{"status":"not_checked"},"fresh_prover":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"fresh_replay":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"index_state":"retained_generated_snapshot"},"guide":{"availability":"available","guide_id":"paper_module.engine_room_demo","plain":"A toolkit built from small modules needs a way to see whether they still cover everything it should. This check is given a list of modules, an example exercise for each, the capabilities the set should cover, and a bad case naming a capability that does not exist. An audit goes through the modules, their exercises and the capabilities they cover, and the outcome is compared with what was expected, including catching the missing capability. It writes a result and validation record, and its tests show that changing one module's example changes the combined result.","plain_availability":"available","ref":"paper_modules/engine_room_demo.md","sha256":"2e1dfe19d72e45448455177084d991503bd020d2fa9207eef5fff4f9bf46e4b9","text":"# Run the Engine Room fixture composition\n\n> **In plain terms.** A toolkit built from small modules needs a way to see whether they still cover everything it should. This check is given a list of modules, an example exercise for each, the capabilities the set should cover, and a bad case naming a capability that does not exist. An audit goes through the modules, their exercises and the capabilities they cover, and the outcome is compared with what was expected, including catching the missing capability. It writes a result and validation record, and its tests show that changing one module's example changes the combined result.\n\nThe Engine Room demo composes bounded fixture checks from several Engine Room modules. Its accepted wrapper runs a controller audit of the configured modules, their fixture exercises and the named capabilities they cover. For example, `bridge_campaign_dag` is one expected capability, called a target in the audit. It writes a result, board and validation receipt, with an optional acceptance receipt.\n\n## Run the example\n\nFrom the repository root, with Python 3.11 or newer, Git and a Lean executable on `PATH` for the Lean fixture:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=src python3 -m microcosm_core.organs.engine_room_demo run \\\n  --input fixtures/first_wave/engine_room_demo/input \\\n  --out .microcosm/component-guides/engine_room_demo \\\n  --acceptance-out .microcosm/component-guides/engine_room_demo/acceptance.json\n```\n\nThe result compares the positive controller audit and a negative case naming a nonexistent target with their expectations. A passing matrix includes detecting the missing target. The component tests also change a subcomponent fixture and check that the composed result changes.\n\nThe wrapper’s acceptance does not by itself admit each individual staged module as an accepted component. Passing this composition describes these public fixtures, not production readiness, complete security or a general theorem prover. [pytest fixtures](https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/reference/fixtures.html) provide background on composing test setup and checks.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe composition includes a Lean exercise for conjunction introduction and disjunction commutativity; it needs Lean on `PATH` and checks the candidate proofs and reported axioms. `make component-replays` also applies the [shared Dafny admission check](../formal/replay/README.md) to the demo’s observed source, input, claim policy and receipt. The direct command above does not invoke that admission check, and neither check proves the demo’s Python composition algorithm.\n\n## Source and evidence\n\n- [Implementation](../src/microcosm_core/organs/engine_room_demo.py) and [composition tests](../tests/test_engine_room_demo.py) and [wrapper tests](../tests/test_engine_room_demo_organ.py).\n- [Fixture inputs](../fixtures/first_wave/engine_room_demo/input/); [historical sample result](../receipts/first_wave/engine_room_demo/engine_room_demo_result.json).\n- [JSON record](../paper_modules/engine_room_demo.json); canonical metadata: [`core/paper_module_capsules.json`](../core/paper_module_capsules.json).\n"},"proofs":[],"replay":{"command":"make component-replays","command_ref":"scripts/check/check_component_replays.py","command_scope":"all registered components","configuration_refs":["src/microcosm_core/runtime_shell.py#RUNTIME_STEPS","src/microcosm_core/runtime_shell.py#_accepted_organ_runner_module_refs"],"declared_prerequisites":{"availability_status":"not_assessed_by_index","description":"Lean, Swift and test extras required","source_ref":"Makefile"},"execution_status":"not_run_by_index","fresh_receipt_template":".microcosm/component-replays/<run>/engine_room_demo/engi